# Wireframe: Header with Connection Status & Notification Badge

## Purpose & Flow Context

The application header displays the WebSocket connection status indicator and notification badge. This is the primary entry point for monitoring real-time connection health and accessing notifications. Entry: app load after authentication. Exit: user navigates away or closes tab.

---

## Notation Legend

| Symbol | Meaning | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|--------|---------|
| `[...]` | Button / interactive element | `[>...▼]` | Dropdown |
| `_______` | Text input / editable field | `[X]` | Close / dismiss |
| `⚠` | Warning / due date | `📎N` | N attachments |
| `💬N` | N comments | `🔗` | Card relationship |
| `👤` | User / mention | `○ ●` | Radio unselected / selected |

## Accessibility — Shared Conventions

All interactive screens inherit these. Per-screen specifics noted where they diverge.

| Concern | Convention |
|---------|------------|
| Landmarks | `header`, `main`, `aside`, `contentinfo` |
| Heading order | One `h1` per screen, `h2` for sections |
| Accessible names | Icon-only controls get `aria-label` |
| Keyboard | Tab, Enter/Space, Escape, Arrow keys |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px reservation |
| Non-color intent | Icon + text, never color alone |

---

## Layout Regions

**Grid**: 12-column layout. Spacing cadence: 8px rhythm intent.

**App-shell**: Shared header + nav + container. Regions:

| Region | Content | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|
| Header | Logo, Navigation, ConnectionStatusIndicator, NotificationBadge, UserMenu | Sticky top, full width |
| Main Content | Page-specific content | Below header, scrollable |
| Sidebar (optional) | Contextual navigation | Hidden on mobile |

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Nav Items]              [● Connected] [🔔3] [Avatar]  |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                    |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|  |                             |  |                             |  |
|  |  {Main Content Area}        |  |  {Sidebar (optional)}       |  |
|  |                             |  |                             |  |
|  +-----------------------------+  +-----------------------------+  |
|                                                                    |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

*Legend: [{Button}] [Input] [Link] [#Heading] [>Dropdown] [Avatar] [Icon]*

## Components & Affordances

| Element | DS Component | Behavior | Edge Cases |
|---------|-------------|----------|------------|
| Logo | Link | Click navigates to home | None |
| Nav Items | Link | Click navigates to section | Active state highlighted |
| ConnectionStatusIndicator | ConnectionStatusIndicator | Shows WebSocket state, click to retry when disconnected | Compact on mobile |
| NotificationBadge | NotificationBadge | Shows unread count, click opens NotificationPanel | Hides when count is 0 |
| UserMenu | Dropdown | Click opens user menu | Keyboard accessible |

## Data Display

This is a navigation header, not a data display screen. The ConnectionStatusIndicator displays connection state, and the NotificationBadge displays unread notification count.

## Content & Microcopy Intent

| Slot | Intent | Notes |
|------|--------|-------|
| ConnectionStatusIndicator text | Communicates connection health | "Connected", "Connecting...", "Reconnecting...", "Disconnected" |
| NotificationBadge count | Shows urgency of unread items | "0" hidden, "1-99" numeric, "99+" for overflow |
| UserMenu trigger | Shows current user | Avatar image or initials |

## States

### Populated (Default — Connected)

The header shows all elements with connection indicator in "connected" state (green dot).

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Nav Items]              [● Connected] [🔔3] [👤]     |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Empty (No Notifications)

Connection indicator shows connected, notification badge hidden.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Nav Items]              [● Connected]      [👤]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Loading (Connecting)

Connection indicator shows "connecting" state with pulse animation.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Nav Items]              [● Connecting...]  [👤]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Error (Disconnected)

Connection indicator shows "disconnected" state (red dot), clickable to retry.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Nav Items]              [● Disconnected]   [👤]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

### Success (Reconnection)

Connection indicator transitions from "reconnecting" to "connected" with brief green flash.

```
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|  [Logo]   [Nav Items]              [● Connected]      [👤]      |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

## Responsive

| Breakpoint | Changes |
|------------|---------|
| Desktop (>1024px) | Full layout as described, all elements visible |
| Tablet (768-1024px) | Nav items may collapse to hamburger, connection status shows text |
| Mobile (<768px) | Nav → hamburger menu, connection status shows dot only (no text), notification badge compact |

## Accessibility — Screen Composition

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| Landmarks | `header` landmark contains all elements |
| Heading order | No headings in header (navigation only) |
| Reading / Focus order | Left to right: Logo → Nav → ConnectionStatus → NotificationBadge → UserMenu |
| Accessible names | ConnectionStatusIndicator: aria-label="Connection status: {state}", NotificationBadge: aria-label="{count} unread notifications" |
| Keyboard operability | Tab through elements, Enter/Space activates, Escape closes dropdowns |
| Target size | ≥24×24 CSS px on all interactive targets |
| Focus not obscured | Header is sticky but doesn't obscure focused elements below |
| Non-color intent | ConnectionStatusIndicator uses dot color + text label |
